## Data Protection

Telemetry and report content produced by PurpleForge is subject to a redaction
pipeline that removes identifiable personal data (email addresses, UK National
Insurance numbers, postcodes, telephone numbers) and secrets (Bearer tokens,
JWTs, AWS access keys, API keys, private key blocks, passwords) at write time.
This supports compliance with the data minimisation and integrity/confidentiality
principles under **UK DPA 2018** and **GDPR Article 5(1)(c) and (f)**.
Operators remain responsible for ensuring that assessment targets are authorised,
that personal data collected during an engagement is handled appropriately, and
that data-subject rights obligations are met.  Redaction is heuristic and does
not guarantee complete removal of all personal data; manual review of logs is
recommended for high-sensitivity engagements.

